{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Vanessa Starts Dating Marco"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "At the Movies"}, {"type": "position", "content": 5}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 9}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe characteristics of different people and their jobs."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations. "}]}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn5le09ob05re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Will, May, Might"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the Future tense (<span class=\"strong\">will</span>) to talk about actions in the future. You can also use the modals <span class=\"strong\">might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">may</span> to talk about possible actions in the future."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We will go see a movie this weekend."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We might have to wait in line to buy tickets."}, {"type": "example", "content": "We may bring our own snacks."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The auxiliary <span class=\"strong\">will</span> goes before the verb. The short form is <span class=\"strong\">\u2018ll</span>.  </br></br>You use the Future tense when you talk about the future, make offers or make predictions.  </br></br>The modals <span class=\"strong\">might</span> and <span class=\"strong\">may</span> go before the verb.  </br></br>They talk about future possibility or a chance that something will happen. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Might</span> means there is a smaller chance that something will happen (30%). </br><span class=\"strong\">May</span> means there is a slightly greater chance that something will happen (50%)."}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Quantifiers"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use a quantifier before a noun to indicate the amount or number of an item."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Are there any comedies playing?"}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are lots of movies to choose from."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I don't think we have enough options to pick from."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use quantifiers with both count and non-count nouns.</br></br> You can use all of the quantifiers below with both count and non-count nouns."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Quantifier\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Meaning\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"more</br> less/fewer</br> no/none </br>any /not any</br> some</br> a lot of / lots of</br> plenty of</br> enough\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"a larger number/amount</br> a smaller number/amount</br> 0, nothing</br> to ask about / say there is not</br> a small number/amount</br> a very large number/amount</br> more than you need</br> as much as you need\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "drama"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a movie that is serious"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I prefer watching dramas."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob05aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about movies."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "comedy"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a movie that is funny"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you want to laugh, you should check out this comedy."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob05aud02"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "sci-fi"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "short for science fiction, a movie about the future related to science "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Did you watch that sci-fi movie about the aliens?"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn5le09ob05aud03"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "historical"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "relating to the past"}, {"type": "part_speech"